# calibrated: the same credential lists the org's members and returns two
# (`gmhelmold`, `cachorronarigudo26-lang`), so the empty teams list is the
# answer, not a permission failure. All ten handles named nobody.
#
# So the handles were replaced with the one reviewer who actually exists,
# @gmhelmold, exactly as the old header instructed. Two consequences, stated
# here so nobody re-derives them:
#
# 1. THIS FILE ENFORCES NOTHING. It was labelled "Source of truth for the
#    'every PR reviewed' GA-Gate criterion" and its catch-all row was labelled
#    "so nothing merges unreviewed". Neither was true. CODEOWNERS only
#    REQUESTS review; requiring it is a branch-protection setting, and on
#    2026-08-31 `GET /repos/HuGR-Labs/corelink-server/branches/main/protection`
#    and `/rulesets` both answered HTTP 403 — "Upgrade to GitHub Pro or make
#    this repository public to enable this feature". Branch protection is not
#    available on this repo's plan at all.
# 2. The sole owner is also the usual author, and GitHub does not request
#    review from the PR author. On most PRs this file requests nothing.
#
# 2026-10-02, org migration: the gmhelmold account was suspended and the
# repository was recreated in the corelink-dev organisation, so every rule now
# routes to @gusmhs, the account that operates corelink-dev. The 2026-08-31
